From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 01:53:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] airconv: Lower IsHelperLane, QuadVote, Msad, the
 sample-position queries and ViewID.

The Shader Model 6.0-6.7 operations a device reporting DXMT's caps must
run, which failed their pipelines as unsupported:

- IsHelperLane (221): air.simd_is_helper_thread in a pixel shader, false
  elsewhere (no other stage has helper lanes).
- QuadVote (222): air.quad_any or air.quad_all, convergent like the
  other simdgroup calls.
- Msad (50): a call of airconv's dxmt.msad.i32, as the DXBC msad
  lowering makes it.
- Texture2DMSGetSamplePosition (75) and RenderTargetGetSamplePosition
  (76): airconv's dxmt.sample_pos.i32 (D3D's standard positions) with
  the texture's or the render target's sample count, split into the
  {f32, f32} result. RenderTargetGetSampleCount (77): air.get_num_samples.
  76 and 77 take no handle, so they no longer go to the resource
  lowering, which failed them as "resource handle through phi/select".
- ViewID (138): 0. View instancing isn't supported, so there is one view.

SM50Initialize sets use_msad and use_samplepos from the module's calls,
so the compiles link the helpers (LinkHelpers). A DXIL geometry
pipeline's object function links the vertex shader's helpers too: it
runs the vertex shader, and upstream links the geometry shader's only
(D3D11 keeps that). Metal compiled the helpers with fast math: the DXIL
float policy (no NaN or infinity assumed away; no reassociation,
contraction or reciprocals before the rasterizer) moves from LowerBody
into StripFastMath, which also runs on a DXIL module after a helper is
linked and drops the helpers' fast-math function attributes. D3D11's
shaders are unchanged.

The op enum also names 75-77, 138, 165-167, 222, 244, 245 and 254-257.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
